WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.800
Fewer false wake-ups

00:00:01.612 --> 00:00:02.696
for a self-hosted

00:00:02.508 --> 00:00:03.510
voice assistant

00:00:04.038 --> 00:00:05.889
Fabio Manganiello swapped

00:00:05.713 --> 00:00:07.587
openWakeWord for microWakeWord

00:00:07.776 --> 00:00:08.802
the engine used

00:00:08.613 --> 00:00:09.922
by ESPHome

00:00:09.946 --> 00:00:10.971
and Home Assistant

00:00:10.783 --> 00:00:11.325
Voice

00:00:11.432 --> 00:00:12.516
in his Platypush

00:00:12.328 --> 00:00:13.165
assistant

00:00:13.702 --> 00:00:15.258
openWakeWord's pre-trained

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:17.133
models were version 0.1

00:00:16.945 --> 00:00:18.737
files from 2023

00:00:18.997 --> 00:00:20.199
mostly trained on

00:00:20.011 --> 00:00:21.084
synthetic speech

00:00:21.249 --> 00:00:22.510
and false triggers

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.053
were high with

00:00:22.865 --> 00:00:23.760
cheap mics

00:00:24.278 --> 00:00:25.362
Now an adaptive

00:00:25.174 --> 00:00:26.542
noise floor ignores

00:00:26.389 --> 00:00:27.402
any frame that

00:00:27.297 --> 00:00:28.039
isn't at least

00:00:27.851 --> 00:00:29.077
twice as loud

00:00:28.889 --> 00:00:29.761
as the tracked

00:00:29.573 --> 00:00:30.575
background level

00:00:30.705 --> 00:00:32.308
roughly six decibels

00:00:32.838 --> 00:00:33.852
Full story on

00:00:33.663 --> 00:00:34.559
the dashboard
